CRITERION 2 — THE CONTRACT TEXT IS TRUE (read from code, not from the comment)
  MET, all three sub-claims.

  (a) "Mode().Perm() ... this function does not thread them through to atomicWrite"
      internal/services/storage/migration.go:280-286 — filePerm does
      `info, err := os.Stat(path)` then `return info.Mode().Perm(), nil`; no special-bit
      handling. Mode().Perm() masks to 0777, so setuid/setgid/sticky are dropped, exactly
      as the comment states.
      The result reaches atomicWrite's chmod in all four helpers
      (`grep -n "filePerm\|atomicWrite" internal/services/storage/migration.go`):
        - encryptFileWithRecipient      : perm at :324 -> s.atomicWrite(path, encrypted, perm) at :333
        - decryptFileWithIdentity       : perm at :371 -> s.atomicWrite(path, decrypted, perm) at :378
        - rollbackEncryptionWithIdentity: perm at :420 -> s.atomicWrite(path, decrypted, perm) at :422
        - rollbackDecryptionWithRecipient: perm at :495 -> s.atomicWrite(path, encrypted, perm) at :497
      No helper reassigns or masks perm between the call and the write.
      internal/services/storage/storage.go:570 atomicWrite applies it verbatim:
      `if err := os.Chmod(tmpPath, perm); err != nil { return err }` before
      `os.Rename(tmpPath, path)`. So the preserved set is precisely the 0777 bits and
      nothing more — the comment describes the actual code.

  (b) "migration only ever rewrites data files ... never executables or directories"
      Both migration walks were read.
      Encrypt path, EnableEncryptionWithProvider (migration.go:55-75): filepath.Walk over
      s.baseDir; `if info.IsDir() { return nil }` skips directories outright; then
      shouldSkipEncryption(path); then `ext := strings.ToLower(filepath.Ext(path))` and the
      file is collected ONLY `if ext == ".csv" || ext == ".json"`. So the rewrite set is
      CSV/JSON data files under the data dir — matching "CSVs, JSON sidecars".
      shouldSkipEncryption (storage.go) further excludes encryption-state files and anything
      under a /cache/ directory (e.g. plotly.min.js).
      Decrypt path, DisableEncryption (migration.go:166-185): same
      `if info.IsDir() { return nil }` directory skip; a file is collected only if
      `isAgeEncrypted(data)` — i.e. only files the encrypt path itself produced, the same
      CSV/JSON set.
      Rollback helpers operate on the already-collected `files` slices from those two walks
      and additionally re-check isAgeEncrypted before rewriting (:394, :468), so they cannot
      widen the set.
      Conclusion: no directory and no non-.csv/.json file is ever passed to
      filePerm/atomicWrite by migration. The comment's factual premise holds.

  (c) "ruling 2026-08-26c"
